  "_comment": "Front-cabin assembly ground truth (flexbody MESH names, not part/slot names) for scoring the detectors. This is the CONFIDENT 26-vehicle torture-test set: every vehicle here has all three roles present AND every mesh confidently placed. Each category lists EVERY mesh that legitimately counts as that assembly across all trims; scoring intersects these with the meshes actually present in a given trim. Scope is the FRONT cabin only: driver+passenger seats (incl. shared racing/vintage seat bases), the dashboard/fascia, and the front (driver+passenger) door cards. Deliberately excluded: rear-row seats, seat bases/rails/legs, door glass/handles/frames/hinges, exterior door moldings/skirts/cladding, and dash accessories (radar, laptop, CB radio, wood/brushed trim, gauges/ornaments). Extracted from vehicles/<name>/**/*.jbeam flexbody rows and hand-curated. Dropped from the full 34: autobello/barstow/midtruck/pigeon/racetruck/wigeon (a role has no distinct mesh) and md_series/nine (seat or door-card meshes not confidently identifiable).",
